WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.467 --> 00:00:16.127
After Zann left, Fala went back upstairs.

2
00:00:16.128 --> 00:00:24.351
Teplo busied himself reading some papers. Perda finished the food Fala had conjured and looked around, feeling restless and worried about Zann.

3
00:00:24.352 --> 00:00:30.353
"I wish we could do something useful," she told Darb. "I hate just sitting here."

4
00:00:30.354 --> 00:00:35.445
Darb didn't answer. He was staring into space. Perda poked him in the arm.

5
00:00:35.446 --> 00:00:41.365
"Huh?" he said. "Oh, sorry. I was just thinking about Zing. I hope he's okay."

6
00:00:41.366 --> 00:00:46.686
"I'm sure he's fine," Perda said. "I wish we could get him back though."

7
00:00:46.687 --> 00:00:50.492
Teplo looked over. "Who are you talking about?"

8
00:00:50.493 --> 00:00:58.681
"Zann's pet dragon," Perda said. "Remember? We told you the palace people took him away when he tried to burn down the door."

9
00:00:58.682 --> 00:01:01.874
Teplo's face lit up. "I think I can help."

10
00:01:01.875 --> 00:01:08.119
He let out a sharp whistle. A moment later they heard a rustle of feathers from a dark corner of the room.

11
00:01:08.120 --> 00:01:12.016
Then a large waterfowl waddled into view.

12
00:01:12.017 --> 00:01:15.180
"What's that?" Darb took a step toward the creature.

13
00:01:15.181 --> 00:01:18.508
"Careful," Teplo said as the bird snapped at Darb.

14
00:01:18.509 --> 00:01:22.083
"She's rather foul-tempered. She's a sniffer goose."

15
00:01:22.084 --> 00:01:28.169
"A what?" Darb looked confused. "I've never heard of that species. Where do they come from?"

16
00:01:28.170 --> 00:01:33.963
"A sniffer goose is a creature whose entire purpose is tracking dragons," Teplo said.

17
00:01:33.964 --> 00:01:38.226
"If you describe Zann's dragon, she should be able to retrieve him."

18
00:01:38.227 --> 00:01:43.715
Perda noticed that the old man hadn't answered Darb's question about where the sniffer goose was from.

19
00:01:43.716 --> 00:01:48.399
But she didn't really care. If they could get Zing back, Zann would be thrilled.

20
00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:54.919
"Zing's a fire whistler," she said. "He's kind of small, with reddish-bronze scales."

21
00:01:54.920 --> 00:01:58.760
She and Darb went on to describe Zing as well as they could.

22
00:01:58.761 --> 00:02:04.302
Teplo listened and translated their description into a series of whistles, grunts, and clicks.

23
00:02:04.303 --> 00:02:06.775
The goose tilted her head and listened.

24
00:02:06.776 --> 00:02:10.800
"You speak this bird's language?" Darb asked, looking impressed.

25
00:02:10.801 --> 00:02:14.944
"I speak sniffer goose well enough to get by." Teplo shrugged.

26
00:02:14.945 --> 00:02:22.335
"It's an easy language to learn. It's even simpler than Troll, and just about anyone can learn that with little trouble."

27
00:02:22.336 --> 00:02:27.456
"If you say so." Perda watched the bird. "Now what happens?"

28
00:02:27.457 --> 00:02:32.764
"Go, my feathered friend!" Teplo fluttered his hands at the goose and let out a honk.

29
00:02:32.765 --> 00:02:36.552
The sniffer goose honked loudly in reply and flapped her wings.

30
00:02:36.553 --> 00:02:39.561
Teplo pulled on a lever, opening the trapdoor.

31
00:02:39.562 --> 00:02:43.991
Honking eagerly, the goose flew up and out.

32
00:02:43.992 --> 00:02:49.765
Teplo closed the trapdoor and smiled at the kids. "Now we wait."

33
00:02:49.766 --> 00:02:56.480
"Who are you?" Zann asked as he floated along behind the mysterious people. "Where are you taking me?"

34
00:02:56.481 --> 00:03:00.897
"Hurry." One of the people shoved Zann's bubble through a doorway.

35
00:03:00.898 --> 00:03:08.524
The bubble touched down and faded, and Zann found himself in a windowless room, face to face with Yog.

36
00:03:08.525 --> 00:03:12.265
Zann gasped. "Did you come to take me back to the palace?"

37
00:03:12.266 --> 00:03:19.122
Yog grinned at him. "Not exactly. But you should have seen Rixa's face when she found out that you four were gone!"

38
00:03:19.123 --> 00:03:27.017
Zann was confused. He glanced at the others, but he didn't recognize any of them. "Then why—"

39
00:03:27.018 --> 00:03:32.073
"Zann!" a woman's voice interrupted. "It's a pleasure to meet you."

40
00:03:32.074 --> 00:03:36.700
Zann turned around. A tall, imposing woman had just entered.

41
00:03:36.701 --> 00:03:42.209
"This is Venna," Yog said. "She's one of the few remaining free members of the Red Council."

42
00:03:42.210 --> 00:03:47.373
Zann had heard of Venna, one of the strongest Magic Masters of her generation.

43
00:03:47.374 --> 00:03:50.179
"Nice to meet you too," he said.

44
00:03:50.180 --> 00:03:54.749
"Sorry we had to grab you off the street like that, Zann," Venna said.

45
00:03:54.750 --> 00:03:57.245
"But it's not safe for you out there.

46
00:03:57.246 --> 00:04:01.783
When I got Teplo's message, I immediately sent my associates to fetch you.

47
00:04:01.784 --> 00:04:06.383
On their way they spotted you and decided to intercept you before the trolls did."

48
00:04:06.384 --> 00:04:09.357
"I was fine," Zann protested.

49
00:04:09.358 --> 00:04:15.257
"Indeed," Venna said. "I'm thrilled that you've eluded the trolls this long.

50
00:04:15.258 --> 00:04:19.128
You must be just as talented as Boz and your parents."

51
00:04:19.129 --> 00:04:24.057
"My parents?" Zann said. "Do—did you know them?"

52
00:04:24.058 --> 00:04:31.991
"Of course! Everyone in First City knew of their fascinating research and mourned the loss of their genius."

53
00:04:31.992 --> 00:04:34.500
Zann wasn't sure what to say to that.

54
00:04:34.501 --> 00:04:38.008
Luckily Venna didn't seem to expect him to say anything.

55
00:04:38.009 --> 00:04:42.377
"That's why I'm so confident you're the right choice," she said.

56
00:04:42.378 --> 00:04:45.745
"The right choice for what?" Zann asked.

57
00:04:45.746 --> 00:04:57.307
Venna smiled. "To become the next king of Magica."

58
00:04:57.308 --> 00:05:03.572
"What do you want?" Morb snapped at the troll who had just entered. "Can't you see that I'm busy?"

59
00:05:03.573 --> 00:05:05.683
The troll didn't respond for a moment.

60
00:05:05.684 --> 00:05:09.922
It stared at Morb's new contraption, fear in its dull eyes.

61
00:05:09.923 --> 00:05:12.913
"Well?" Morb said impatiently.

62
00:05:12.914 --> 00:05:16.017
The troll finally looked at him and let out a grunt.

63
00:05:16.018 --> 00:05:19.748
An image formed briefly above its head and then sputtered out.

64
00:05:19.749 --> 00:05:27.935
Morb frowned. "Was that the boy—Boz's grandson?" he demanded. "Did you idiots finally capture him?"

65
00:05:27.936 --> 00:05:34.543
The troll shook its head. Another puff of magical energy showed Zann with a crown on his head.

66
00:05:34.544 --> 00:05:40.179
"What?" Morb exclaimed. "They're making him king? Impossible!"

67
00:05:40.180 --> 00:05:44.251
The troll grunted, but Morb had never bothered to learn its language.

68
00:05:44.252 --> 00:05:51.002
Morb was tempted to stop what he was doing to find out more but he decided against it. Soon it wouldn't matter.

69
00:05:51.003 --> 00:05:53.892
Morb looked at his contraption with satisfaction.

70
00:05:53.893 --> 00:05:58.999
The pythons the old woman had brought were writhing in a large glass tube in the middle.

71
00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:03.454
The bone-and-wire frame filled most of the space in the underground room.

72
00:06:03.455 --> 00:06:11.226
Soon, very soon now, it would be time to move it to a larger location, and Morb had a particular spot in mind.

73
00:06:11.227 --> 00:06:14.121
There Morb would have more space to work.

74
00:06:14.122 --> 00:06:21.453
There he would be able to find the few remaining parts he needed.
